\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Example}
\title{One trace under full and prefix-window attention}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{diagram}
\tag{schematic}

\p{This schematic keeps the model and token history fixed while changing only
the retained-context policy. It is a local illustration, not a source figure.}

\tikzfig{\begin{tikzpicture}[
 box/.style={draw,rounded corners,align=center,text width=28mm,
 minimum height=10mm,font=\small},arr/.style={->,>=stealth,semithick}]
\node[box] (h) at (-3.6,0) {prompt + trace};
\node[box] (full) at (0,1.3) {full history\\decoder};
\node[box] (win) at (0,-1.3) {prefix + recent window\\decoder};
\node[box] (yf) at (3.6,1.3) {continuation};
\node[box] (yw) at (3.6,-1.3) {continuation};
\draw[arr] (h)--(full); \draw[arr] (h)--(win);
\draw[arr] (full)--(yf); \draw[arr] (win)--(yw);
\end{tikzpicture}}

\p{The two outputs can differ even though the represented weights and visible
prompt are identical. Any claim about improvement must therefore name the
retained-context intervention and its evaluation law.}
